    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e0c5acae_4d07e8a1",
        "filename": "drivers/staging/android/virt_wifi.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 208,
      "author": {
        "id": 1381006
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T00:17:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Generally speaking, you want to order big-\u003esmall, except word-sized members should be placed at the top because those buckets can never be better filled (think bin-packing).  This gets tricky with struct-within-struct (opacity, expansion, etc).  Something like the below seems reasonable to me:\n\n\tstruct virt_wifi_netdev_priv {\n\t\tstruct net_device *lowerdev;\n\t\tstruct net_device *upperdev;\n\t\tu32 tx_packets;\n\t\tu32 tx_failed;\n\t\tstruct delayed_work connect;\n\t\tu8 connect_requested_bss[ETH_ALEN];\n\t\tbool being_deleted;\n\t\tbool is_connected;\n\t\tbool is_up;\n\t};\n\nThe above assumes you\u0027re doing this for memory-efficiency reasons, though.  If you need run-time performance, then you can make that trade-off and waste space as needed for important members.",
      "parentUuid": "de8df895_427afdac",
      "revId": "9222f683679b26ff23788e888706451c3b2caafa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "89577424_422bde1f",
        "filename": "drivers/staging/android/virt_wifi.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 208,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291337
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T00:54:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the explanation! The only times this struct is referenced on the critical path are in virt_wifi_start_xmit and virt_wifi_rx_handler, since those are invoked per-packet in the networking level. Those functions use is_connected, lowerdev, upperdev, tx_packets, and tx_failed. I\u0027ll move is_connected to the top to guarantee alignment, and otherwise use your recommended layout, assuming the pointers get word-aligned after the bool.",
      "parentUuid": "e0c5acae_4d07e8a1",
      "revId": "9222f683679b26ff23788e888706451c3b2caafa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
